489-b43f-fbb9222cdc20","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Root cause recorded in the description (2026-11-21 PST), from the run 44681457334 JUnit tracebacks read against origin/main 863abe7cd19. 4 product defects, 1 of them data-destructive on Windows: compaction recovery stores the snapshot path with a backslash (compact_recovery.py:50) and probes git cat-file -e HEAD:<that path> (:94), so a committed fold reads as absent and is reverted; test_recovery_discards_journal_when_snapshot_is_committed observed recover_abandoned_folds_locked() == 1 on Windows. The other 3 (search_files hits, a code-review error path, two repo scripts) print native paths where a POSIX repo-relative path is the contract. The remaining failures are test-side spelling comparisons; 2 Seatbelt profile tests are macOS-only by subject.","timestamp":1795257798582963001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan-review advisory accepted (verified against scripts/mutation_sandbox.py _sb_quote): test_profile_denies_writes_then_permits_the_allow_list never runs sandbox-exec; it fails on Windows because the profile escapes each backslash of the path while the test expects the raw path. It is fixed by comparing with the escaped form, not skipped. Only test_profile_escapes_quotes_and_backslashes_in_paths stays intentionally unsupported (a directory name containing a double quote is invalid on Windows, WinError 123). Evidence for the on-main ACs comes from the scheduled main sweep after merge; the tmp/w3-owl run is the pre-push check.","timestamp":1795258793268590001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Windows run 44900397644 (tmp/w3-owl at f9e8e7d4c51, rebased on origin/main 1a11014a3a4; sweep (windows) job 136835503555): 5 failed, 20492 passed, 892 skipped. All 40 removed tests, the new native-separator journal test and test_recovery_discards_journal_when_snapshot_is_committed passed. The 5 failures are outside this class: test_check_verify_host x3 (consummate-amethyst-bull) and test_git_metrics x2 (cloth-osmophilic-izuthrush).","timestamp":1795267769197337001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"make verify passed on f9e8e7d4c51 (log /Users/joeoakhart/rebar/.rebar/worktrees/w3-owl/.rebar/scratch/s05f74084-w3/make-verify.log: 21650 passed, 31 skipped default tier; 226 passed, 2 skipped integration tier).","timestamp":1795272329462867001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Gerrit 3512 submitted at revision f9e8e7d4c51 (LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, 0 unresolved); merged on origin/main as da0c6a6ab8f. Waiting for the next scheduled main sweep (windows) to record AC1/AC3 evidence.","timestamp":1795277384533080001}],"created_at":1795154021446724001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"36ca6b10-a8d4-4edb-9440-e1ec66839cc7","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"8aa0-2120-5ef3-4750"},{"link_uuid":"a53370b3-9640-4584-ad83-5293b203fb2b","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"ec7c-7ee2-f48d-4780"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nDiscovered while triaging breezy-hogged-mastiff, which owns `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/unclassified.args`. These 41 entries move to `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/path-separators.args`, which this bug owns.\n\nSome cases are product output that should be POSIX-form: the agent `search_files` tool prints `pkg\\alpha.py:2:` (`test_pai_tools_search_files_bf31.py`, `test_pydantic_ai_runner.py`), the compaction intent journal records `<tid>\\x-SNAPSHOT.json` (`test_compact_crash_atomicity.py`), and the code-review prompt error names `.rebar\\prompts\\...` (`test_code_review_project_criteria.py`). Others are test fakes or expectations: the replacement-walker fake reducer splits paths on `/` while the product joins with `os.path.join` (`tests/unit/commands/test_replacement_walker.py:33`), the AST-guard tests compare `relative_to` output with `jira_family/` (`test_jira_family_boundary.py`, `test_rich_text_seam.py`), and POSIX container paths pass through `Path` (`test_gate_scratch_volume_aa40.py::test_autodeploy_mcp_run_new_routes_gate_scratch_to_the_parent_bind`).\n\nEvidence: Windows runs on throwaway branch `tmp/w05-remeasure` with origin/main `717c50f8b33` code plus a selection-only workflow change: run 44665461131 (the 242 `unclassified.args` entries; 48 passed, 194 failed or errored) and run 44681457334 (the 194, xdist, JUnit XML with full tracebacks). Both 2026-11-19 PST.\n\n## Root cause (established 2026-11-21 PST from the run 44681457334 tracebacks and the code at origin/main `863abe7cd19`)\nProduct defects (a native `\\`-separated path where a POSIX repo-relative path is the contract):\n1. **Compaction recovery reverts a fold that already committed (data-destructive).** `write_intent` stores `os.path.relpath(...)` (`src/rebar/_commands/compact_recovery.py:50-51`), so on Windows the journal reads `<tid>\\x-SNAPSHOT.json`. `_snapshot_in_head` then probes `git cat-file -e HEAD:<tid>\\x-SNAPSHOT.json` (`:94`); git tree paths use `/`, so a committed snapshot reads as absent and recovery reverts the landed fold. `test_recovery_discards_journal_when_snapshot_is_committed` shows exactly that: `recover_abandoned_folds_locked` returned 1 (a revert) where 0 is required.\n2. Agent `search_files` hits use `os.path.relpath` (`src/rebar/llm/pai_tools.py:150`), so the model is shown `pkg\\alpha.py:2:`; the sibling `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/read_set.py:172` already uses `PurePath(...).as_posix()`.\n3. The code-review project-criterion error formats `Path(\".rebar\") / \"prompts\" / ...` (`src/rebar/llm/code_review/batch_runner.py:304`) natively.\n4. `scripts/check_templatefile_escapes.py:175` resolves a non-literal `templatefile()` path by `str(p).endswith(suffix)` with a `/` suffix, so on Windows the `sso-gate` call site is reported unresolvable (\"SILENTLY UNGUARDED\"); its reports (`:211`, `:233`) and `scripts/check_user_data_size.py:176,198` (which reuses `resolve_template_path`, hence the `StopIteration` in `test_user_data_size_a68c.py`) print native paths. This is the rule commit `f163c9c987f` applied to six other repo scripts.\n\nTest-side defects (product behaviour is correct on Windows): a fake reducer splitting on `/` (`test_replacement_walker.py:33`); `/jira-dig-1/` substring matches on native event paths (`test_inbound_status_cascade.py`); `str(relative_to)` compared with POSIX literals (`test_reconcile_once.py:434`, `test_jira_family_boundary.py:269`, `test_rich_text_seam.py:163,203`, `test_project_review_phase_boundaries.py:212`); a native absolute path compared with git's `C:/` form (`test_rebar_repo_isolation.py:88-99`, `test_relocated_store_repo_root.py:446`); `str(path) in message` where the message shows `repr(path)` by design (`src/rebar/llm/criteria/overlay.py:139-145`, `test_prompt_repo_root_seam.py`); an absolute overlay path (`snapshot.py:223`) checked with a POSIX `endswith` (`test_criteria_snapshot.py:112`); a Windows path written into a TOML basic string, where `\\U` is an escape (`test_worktree_config_root.py:240`); and a POSIX container mount passed through `Path` (`test_gate_scratch_volume_aa40.py:285-298`).\n\nIntentionally unsupported: `test_mutation_sandbox.py::test_profile_denies_writes_then_permits_the_allow_list` and `::test_profile_escapes_quotes_and_backslashes_in_paths` test the macOS Seatbelt profile builder (`sandbox-exec` exists only on macOS; the second needs a directory name containing `\"`, which Windows forbids, WinError 123).\n\n## Approach\n- Product: emit POSIX repo-relative paths at the 4 boundaries with `PurePath(...).as_posix()` / `Path.as_posix()`. In compaction recovery, write the journal POSIX and also convert the stored path with `PurePath(rel).as_posix()` at the `git cat-file` probe, so a journal written before the fix on Windows is still read correctly (on POSIX `PurePath` keeps a literal `\\`, so behaviour there is unchanged). `os.path.join(tracker, \"a/b\")` already works on Windows, so the restore paths need no change.\n- Tests: compare paths structurally (`Path(...).parent.name`, `.as_posix()`, `os.path.realpath`, `repr(...)`, `PurePosixPath`), never by native string spelling.\n- Skip the 2 Seatbelt profile tests on Windows (`sys.platform == \"win32\"`) with that reason; their lines stay in `path-separators.args`, recorded here.\n- No new config key, env var, flag or dependency.\n\n## Scope\nProduct: `src/rebar/_commands/compact_recovery.py`, `src/rebar/llm/pai_tools.py`, `src/rebar/llm/code_review/batch_runner.py`, `scripts/check_templatefile_escapes.py`, `scripts/check_user_data_size.py`. Tests: `tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py`, `tests/scripts/test_mutation_sandbox.py`, `tests/unit/commands/test_replacement_walker.py`, `tests/unit/reconciler/mutate/test_inbound_status_cascade.py`, `tests/unit/reconciler/orchestrate/test_reconcile_once.py`, `tests/unit/reconciler/test_jira_family_boundary.py`, `tests/unit/reconciler/test_rich_text_seam.py`, `tests/unit/test_criteria_snapshot.py`, `tests/unit/test_gate_scratch_volume_aa40.py`, `tests/unit/test_project_review_phase_boundaries.py`, `tests/unit/test_prompt_repo_root_seam.py`, `tests/unit/test_relocated_store_repo_root.py`, `tests/unit/test_worktree_config_root.py`, `tests/unit/test_compact_crash_atomicity.py` (one new test), and `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/path-separators.args`.\n\n## Testing\n- The 39 fixed tests are the regression tests for the product fixes on Windows (they fail there today with the output quoted above). They pass on macOS before and after, since POSIX paths are unchanged.\n- New test in `test_compact_crash_atomicity.py`: a journal whose snapshot path is written with the native separator (`os.path.join(tid, \"x-SNAPSHOT.json\")`) for a committed snapshot makes recovery return 0 and keep the snapshot. On Windows that is the pre-fix journal shape; on POSIX it is identical to the POSIX form.\n- A `sweep (windows)` run of the exact tree on `tmp/w3-owl`, then `make verify` through the verify-slot queue.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every line removed from `path-separators.args` names a test that passed in a `sweep (windows)` run on main after the fix (run id recorded in a comment).\n- [ ] `path-separators.args` is empty and deleted with its reference in `.github/workflows/test.yml`, or each remaining line names a test recorded on this ticket as intentionally unsupported on Windows with the reason.\n- [ ] `test_recovery_discards_journal_when_snapshot_is_committed` and the new native-separator journal test pass in that `sweep (windows)` run (run id recorded in a comment).\n- [ ] `make verify` passes on the pushed tree (log path recorded in a comment).","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/compact_recovery.py","reason":"emit POSIX repo-relative paths"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/pai_tools.py","reason":"emit POSIX repo-relative paths"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/code_review/batch_runner.py","reason":"emit POSIX repo-relative paths"},{"path":"scripts/check_templatefile_escapes.py","reason":"emit POSIX repo-relative paths"},{"path":"scripts/check_user_data_size.py","reason":"emit POSIX repo-relative paths"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py","reason":"compare paths structurally, not by native spelling"},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_mutation_sandbox.py","reason":"compare paths structurally, not by native spelling"},{"path":"tests/unit/commands/test_replacement_walker.py","reason":"compare paths structurally, not by native spelling"},{"path":"tests/unit/reconciler/mutate/test_inbound_status_cascade.py","reason":"compare paths structurally, not by native spelling"},{"path":"tests/unit/reconciler/orchestrate/test_reconcile_once.py","reason":"compare paths structurally, not by native spelling"},{"path":"tests/unit/reconciler/test_jira_family_boundary.py","reason":"compare paths structurally, not by native spelling"},{"path":"tests/unit/reconciler/test_rich_text_seam.py","reason":"compare paths structurally, not by native spelling"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_criteria_snapshot.py","reason":"compare paths structurally, not by native spelling"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_gate_scratch_volume_aa40.py","reason":"compare paths structurally, not by native spelling"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_project_review_phase_boundaries.py","reason":"compare paths structurally, not by native spelling"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_prompt_repo_root_seam.py","reason":"compare paths structurally, not by native spelling"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_relocated_store_repo_root.py","reason":"compare paths structurally, not by native spelling"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_worktree_config_root.py","reason":"compare paths structurally, not by native spelling"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_compact_crash_atomicity.py","reason":"compare paths structurally, not by native spelling"},{"path":".github/windows-sweep-deselect/path-separators.args","reason":"remove each line whose test passes on Windows"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[["relates_to","ec7c-7ee2-f48d-4780"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"1976efee-eb90-4d8d-aa90-67a34e224aa9","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["windows","portability"],"ticket_id":"7a2d-9166-ce30-4c1d","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Windows sweep: 41 tests still compare backslash paths with forward-slash expectations","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["c8dbde5f-3a95-40bf-bae2-741d566d0535","19c34be3-3c3a-4b8c-aec0-96b85a14949e","